From 4040b85e05b2a92a47ecc40a45f90b32c6293131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:58:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: an animation catches up every iteration a gap
 skipped

A resolve advanced each CSS animation by at most one iteration. After a
gap longer than an iteration (an embedder that did not resolve for a
while, a stalled frame), the animation's start stayed iterations behind,
its progress clamped to the end of the current one, and it showed its
last keyframe until enough resolves had caught it up, one iteration
each.

Iterate until the iteration in progress is the one the time falls in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo/traversal.rs | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo/traversal.rs b/packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo/traversal.rs
index 06cde0035..0cea284d1 100644
--- a/packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo/traversal.rs
+++ b/packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo/traversal.rs
@@ -79,7 +79,10 @@ impl crate::document::BaseDocument {
                 if animation.state == AnimationState::Pending && animation.started_at <= now {
                     animation.state = AnimationState::Running;
                 }
-                animation.iterate_if_necessary(now);
+                // Every iteration that ended since the last resolve: one
+                // resolve after a gap longer than an iteration must not
+                // show the end of an old one.
+                while animation.iterate_if_necessary(now) {}
 
                 if animation.state == AnimationState::Running && animation.has_ended(now) {
                     animation.state = AnimationState::Finished;
